          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Academic and Public Service</strong><br>\nIn addition to his UN work, Bunche served as a professor at Howard University, where he influenced many students. His academic work complemented his diplomatic efforts, reinforcing his belief in the power of education to foster international understanding.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Honors and Memorials</strong><br>\nThroughout his life, Bunche received numerous honors for his contributions to peace and civil rights. He received the Presidential Medal of Freedom and was commemorated in various ways, including schools named in his honor.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Ralph Bunche's Enduring Legacy</strong><br>\nRalph Bunche passed away in 1971, but his legacy as a diplomat and peacemaker endures. His work at the United Nations set a precedent for peace negotiations, and his commitment to civil rights remains an inspiration to all who advocate for peace and justice.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
